// SOURCE: examples/errors-and-results/main.tach
// FLAGS: --check-alloc
// STDIN: name = demo
// STDIN: port = 8080
// STDIN: colour = blue
// EXPECT: rejected samples:
// EXPECT:   "port = 80\nport = 81"     line 2: `port` is set twice
// EXPECT:   "port: 80"                 line 1: expected `key = value`
// EXPECT:   "port = 80\ncolour = blue" line 2: unknown key `colour`
// EXPECT:   "port = 8o"                line 1: port: not a number (invalid digit at byte 1)
// EXPECT:   "port = 70000"             line 1: port: 70000 is not in 1..=65535
// EXPECT:   "port = 80\ndebug = yes"   line 2: debug: expected true or false
// EXPECT:   "name = no port"           `port` is required
// EXIT: 1
// STDERR: Error: UnknownKey(3, "colour")
// (0.17: the error owns a copy of its key, so main can drop the input
// it read before its caller prints the error; --check-alloc finds no
// leak and no use of freed memory.)
